<title>USA: Chile buys Cabinda, Zaire crudes for mid-March.</title>
<headline>Chile buys Cabinda, Zaire crudes for mid-March.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile's state-owned oil company Empresa Nacional del Petroleo (ENAP) bought two West African crudes for mid-March in its latest purchase tender, trade sources said on Thursday.</p>
<p>ENAP bought 600,000 barrels of Cabinda and 350,000 barrels of Zaire crude from a U.S. company, the sources said.</p>
<p>The crudes were priced off of dated Brent.</p>
<p>Cabinda is a low-sulfur crude with an API gravity of 32 degrees. Zaire is of similar quality.</p>
<p>Earlier today, Uruguay bought Suez Blend crude for late March delivery in its latest purchase tender.</p>
<p>--Patricia Garip-Bertuol NY Energy Desk ((+1 212 859 1620))</p>
